00:00:00,010 --> 00:00:35
[ Watch on kissFlix.co ]

1
00:00:00,305 --> 00:00:01,305
(All characters and organisations in this drama are fictional.)

2
00:00:01,305 --> 00:00:02,645
(Filming with minors followed broadcast guidelines,)

3
00:00:02,645 --> 00:00:03,675
(and generative AI was used in select scenes.)

4
00:00:16,591 --> 00:00:19,631
- This looks amazing. - Enjoy.

5
00:00:37,281 --> 00:00:38,581
Is kimchi fried rice...

6
00:00:39,121 --> 00:00:40,281
your comfort food?

7
00:00:40,551 --> 00:00:41,551
Yes.

8
00:00:42,321 --> 00:00:43,821
When I eat kimchi fried rice,

9
00:00:45,321 --> 00:00:47,831
all my stress and worries just disappear.

10
00:00:48,391 --> 00:00:52,301
My sadness melts away like snow. It's magical, isn't it?

11
00:00:54,431 --> 00:00:56,631
Well, I'm a little jealous,

12
00:00:57,271 --> 00:00:58,771
but okay, noted.

13
00:01:02,011 --> 00:01:03,211
This is so delicious.

14
00:01:03,711 --> 00:01:05,381
How are you such a good cook?

15
00:01:06,141 --> 00:01:08,411
Of all the kimchi fried rice I've ever had,

16
00:01:08,711 --> 00:01:11,111
this is the best of the best.

17
00:01:11,551 --> 00:01:12,551
The best.

18
00:01:13,921 --> 00:01:17,151
I'll make you kimchi fried rice every day from now on.

19
00:01:19,221 --> 00:01:21,161
Have I hit the jackpot, Han Gyu Rim?

20
00:01:22,331 --> 00:01:23,861
Am I allowed to be this happy?

21
00:01:24,191 --> 00:01:25,201
Are you happy?

22
00:01:26,361 --> 00:01:27,361
Me too.

23
00:01:29,301 --> 00:01:30,431
It's so good.

24
00:01:33,471 --> 00:01:35,871
We don't normally prepare off-menu items,

25
00:01:36,641 --> 00:01:38,711
but I'm making a special exception just for you.

26
00:01:43,851 --> 00:01:44,981
Thank you.

27
00:01:45,481 --> 00:01:47,751
Enjoy your meal.

28
00:02:26,821 --> 00:02:27,821
Chef.

29
00:02:28,561 --> 00:02:30,131
This is completely burnt. Goodness.

30
00:03:47,741 --> 00:03:48,741
Chef.

31
00:03:54,141 --> 00:03:56,981
Right now, the entire staff is walking on eggshells around you.

32
00:04:01,221 --> 00:04:03,591
Chug some ice water and get a grip.

33
00:04:04,321 --> 00:04:06,591
- Yes. - Goodness.

34
00:04:08,161 --> 00:04:09,261
What was I just doing?

35
00:04:09,331 --> 00:04:11,431
You were just burning the salmon, Chef.

36
00:04:24,711 --> 00:04:27,011
From now on, we will not be making off-menu dishes.

37
00:04:27,081 --> 00:04:28,081
Ever.

38
00:04:33,721 --> 00:04:36,321
That was delicious. Thank you.

39
00:04:51,131 --> 00:04:52,141
Gyu Rim.

40
00:04:57,371 --> 00:04:59,641
Please don't come back to our restaurant again.

41
00:05:01,211 --> 00:05:02,211
Why?

42
00:05:02,481 --> 00:05:03,651
You know why.

43
00:05:05,981 --> 00:05:06,981
What do you mean?

44
00:05:07,281 --> 00:05:08,291
Why are you suddenly acting like this?

45
00:05:08,291 --> 00:05:09,551
It's not like you, Gyu Rim.

46
00:05:12,921 --> 00:05:15,831
Fine. I won't come again...

47
00:05:17,361 --> 00:05:19,001
I should have taken the hint.

48
00:05:19,961 --> 00:05:21,161
Is that what I'm supposed to say?

49
00:05:22,301 --> 00:05:24,131
If I were the Han Gyu Rim you used to know.

50
00:05:25,201 --> 00:05:26,271
Exactly.

51
00:05:27,671 --> 00:05:29,171
That's the kind of person you were, Gyu Rim.

52
00:05:29,271 --> 00:05:30,611
Suddenly showing up like this,

53
00:05:30,671 --> 00:05:32,441
making things awkward, and stirring up trouble,

54
00:05:32,511 --> 00:05:33,741
causing a meltdown...

55
00:05:34,141 --> 00:05:35,811
That absurd behaviour wasn't like you.

56
00:05:37,811 --> 00:05:39,251
Why can't I?

57
00:05:41,721 --> 00:05:42,721
What?

58
00:05:43,251 --> 00:05:44,861
Making people uncomfortable,

59
00:05:45,461 --> 00:05:46,721
stirring up trouble,

60
00:05:47,361 --> 00:05:48,861
and causing a meltdown...

61
00:05:49,961 --> 00:05:51,801
Other people do it all the time.

62
00:05:53,461 --> 00:05:56,771
Why am I not allowed to do it?

63
00:05:58,341 --> 00:05:59,341
Well...

64
00:06:01,571 --> 00:06:03,441
Seriously, why are you suddenly being like this?

65
00:06:03,941 --> 00:06:05,011
I wouldn't care if it were anyone else,

66
00:06:05,011 --> 00:06:06,081
but coming from you, Gyu Rim,

67
00:06:06,681 --> 00:06:08,311
it completely baffles me.

68
00:06:10,851 --> 00:06:12,381
Just for once,

69
00:06:13,421 --> 00:06:15,651
I want to stop caring what other people think...

70
00:06:17,091 --> 00:06:18,591
and just be selfish.

71
00:06:19,761 --> 00:06:23,991
Forgetting what I've done, the pain I've caused,

72
00:06:25,531 --> 00:06:27,301
and all of my mistakes,

73
00:06:28,201 --> 00:06:30,371
and just be brazenly shameless.

74
00:06:32,801 --> 00:06:34,541
Can't I live my life that way?

75
00:06:36,811 --> 00:06:38,681
To stop holding back for once,

76
00:06:39,581 --> 00:06:41,211
to stop being so considerate,

77
00:06:42,451 --> 00:06:44,251
and just follow my heart...

78
00:06:46,781 --> 00:06:47,951
If I lived like that,

79
00:06:49,851 --> 00:06:51,191
would that be so wrong?

80
00:07:15,881 --> 00:07:16,881
Of course not.

81
00:07:17,751 --> 00:07:19,151
Of course you can. Absolutely.

82
00:07:20,321 --> 00:07:22,891
It's a free country. Why couldn't you?

83
00:07:23,691 --> 00:07:25,021
You're only human, Gyu Rim.

84
00:07:46,741 --> 00:07:49,411
You must have missed her a lot. You did well to hold back.

85
00:07:49,951 --> 00:07:51,351
I was on edge, wondering if you were going to...

86
00:07:51,351 --> 00:07:52,981
insist on serving her yourself.

87
00:07:53,821 --> 00:07:54,821
Got a smoke?

88
00:07:54,991 --> 00:07:58,291
A smoke? Why all of a sudden? You quit when you started cooking.

89
00:07:59,161 --> 00:08:00,521
Do you have a smoke or not?

90
00:08:02,591 --> 00:08:05,261
No. I smoked them all. I need to go buy some too.

91
00:08:06,961 --> 00:08:08,471
Think anyone else has a cigarette?

92
00:08:10,331 --> 00:08:11,771
You were totally thrown, weren't you?

93
00:08:12,371 --> 00:08:13,941
I was totally floored too.

94
00:08:14,471 --> 00:08:16,241
I never dreamed Gyu Rim would show up...

95
00:08:16,241 --> 00:08:17,611
at our restaurant.

96
00:08:17,611 --> 00:08:19,111
I'm going to go buy some smokes.

97
00:08:20,111 --> 00:08:22,311
If it's this hard, just break up with Seo Hyun.

98
00:08:22,381 --> 00:08:24,011
Break up with Seo Hyun and go to Han Gyu Rim.

99
00:08:24,081 --> 00:08:25,121
Han Gyu Rim, too,

100
00:08:25,681 --> 00:08:27,781
seems like a complete mess because she can't get over you.

101
00:08:28,051 --> 00:08:30,721
I just want a smoke. What's with all this nonsense?

102
00:08:30,791 --> 00:08:32,321
You want to go to Gyu Rim.

103
00:08:35,931 --> 00:08:38,231
Let's be real, you don't feel a thing for Seo Hyun.

104
00:08:39,201 --> 00:08:41,561
I know you feel you have to keep your word to Seo Hyun,

105
00:08:41,631 --> 00:08:43,331
but so what if you can't?

106
00:08:44,631 --> 00:08:46,871
Besides, Seo Hyun's mother is dead set against it.

107
00:08:47,241 --> 00:08:49,511
Not everyone keeps their word like you do.

108
00:08:49,511 --> 00:08:52,341
Hey, how many cigarettes are you smoking a day?

109
00:08:52,711 --> 00:08:54,841
The pack was brand new this morning. Did you smoke it all already?

110
00:08:54,981 --> 00:08:57,451
You'll fry your brain, and your bones will crumble.

111
00:08:57,581 --> 00:08:59,181
Are you trying to die young?

112
00:08:59,381 --> 00:09:01,251
What's the point of working out...

113
00:09:01,321 --> 00:09:03,051
and taking vitamins with an attitude like that?

114
00:09:03,621 --> 00:09:05,421
You idiot.

115
00:09:07,161 --> 00:09:10,631
Hey. You're quitting smoking, starting right now.

116
00:09:10,991 --> 00:09:14,301
A chain-smoking restaurant owner? Seriously?

117
00:09:14,561 --> 00:09:18,171
Don't even think about not quitting. Or you're fired tomorrow. Got it?

118
00:09:26,141 --> 00:09:28,681
Right, you have to take it out on me.

119
00:09:29,311 --> 00:09:31,981
You have to take your frustrations out on me to feel better.

120
00:09:32,181 --> 00:09:34,521
Dear Lord.

121
00:09:35,121 --> 00:09:37,391
Why do you keep sending me all these crazy people...

122
00:09:37,451 --> 00:09:39,461
and putting me...

123
00:09:40,121 --> 00:09:42,291
through these ordeals?

124
00:09:45,901 --> 00:09:47,761
If he tells me to quit, I have to quit.

125
00:10:20,201 --> 00:10:21,661
I wanted to see you.

126
00:10:25,771 --> 00:10:27,771
You could have at least shown your face.

127
00:10:31,141 --> 00:10:32,211
Does this mean...

128
00:10:34,781 --> 00:10:36,451
I should never come back?

129
00:10:58,131 --> 00:10:59,671
Don't ever come back, Han Gyu Rim.

130
00:11:01,741 --> 00:11:03,171
I won't make it for you again.

131
00:11:07,311 --> 00:11:08,711
I understand what you mean...

132
00:11:10,881 --> 00:11:12,281
perfectly.

133
00:11:14,721 --> 00:11:15,851
Still...

134
00:11:20,921 --> 00:11:22,431
The kimchi fried rice...

135
00:11:28,261 --> 00:11:30,171
was absolutely delicious.

136
00:11:33,801 --> 00:11:34,941
Thank you...

137
00:11:37,241 --> 00:11:38,441
so, so much...

138
00:11:41,711 --> 00:11:43,011
for everything.

139
00:12:03,201 --> 00:12:04,801
Gyu Rim went to Mu Jin's restaurant?

140
00:12:05,101 --> 00:12:06,871
Yes, and she ordered kimchi fried rice,

141
00:12:06,871 --> 00:12:08,541
which isn't even on the menu.

142
00:12:08,641 --> 00:12:10,871
And Mu Jin made it for her. Can you believe it?

143
00:12:11,111 --> 00:12:13,011
Is Gyu Rim still in love with Mu Jin?

144
00:12:14,181 --> 00:12:15,181
You didn't know?

145
00:12:16,951 --> 00:12:19,681
What about Mu Jin? How does he feel about her?

146
00:12:20,681 --> 00:12:23,521
His staff says he's seeing someone.

147
00:12:23,821 --> 00:12:25,421
Come on. Just because there's a goalie...

148
00:12:25,491 --> 00:12:26,691
doesn't mean you can't score.

149
00:12:27,421 --> 00:12:29,131
I don't know about the goalie,

150
00:12:29,191 --> 00:12:31,361
but that goalpost is ridiculously strong.

151
00:12:31,691 --> 00:12:34,801
His defence is insane, and there's no opening for a shot.

152
00:12:34,861 --> 00:12:37,601
Then why did she break up with him if she liked him so much?

153
00:12:38,401 --> 00:12:41,301
Hey, why do you think they broke up?

154
00:12:41,701 --> 00:12:45,681
You, me, Dad, Han Gyu Young, and Han Gyu Oh.

155
00:12:46,281 --> 00:12:48,951
It must have been because of our awful family.

156
00:12:49,011 --> 00:12:52,121
- She didn't want to drag him down. - Really?

157
00:12:52,421 --> 00:12:53,881
It was because of our family?

158
00:12:55,521 --> 00:12:58,691
You're brilliantly smart about some things,

159
00:12:58,791 --> 00:13:01,791
but for others, you're hopelessly clueless. You know?

160
00:13:02,131 --> 00:13:04,031
You petty brats.

161
00:13:04,431 --> 00:13:06,301
Hey, if you were already washing clothes,

162
00:13:06,361 --> 00:13:08,101
couldn't you have hung mine up to dry too?

163
00:13:10,271 --> 00:13:11,271
You specifically chose my clothes...

164
00:13:11,331 --> 00:13:12,941
and just left them in the washing machine.

165
00:13:13,101 --> 00:13:15,241
Since the laundry was already running,

166
00:13:15,311 --> 00:13:17,141
we washed them together to save water.

167
00:13:17,341 --> 00:13:19,711
You can hang your own clothes up to dry, Dad.

168
00:13:19,841 --> 00:13:22,511
If you're going to live with Gyu Oh, you need to practice now, don't you?

169
00:13:22,581 --> 00:13:24,551
Here, shake them out like this. Shake them.

170
00:13:25,051 --> 00:13:26,521
I'm not living with Gyu Oh.

171
00:13:27,021 --> 00:13:28,751
I'm going to live with Gyu Rim, Gyeol, and you kids.

172
00:13:28,921 --> 00:13:29,991
Says who?

173
00:13:30,221 --> 00:13:31,791
If you all abandon me,

174
00:13:32,121 --> 00:13:33,491
the whole neighbourhood will find out.

175
00:13:33,561 --> 00:13:35,891
They'll say you're the most ungrateful children alive.

176
00:13:36,061 --> 00:13:37,061
Hey, if that rumour spreads,

177
00:13:37,131 --> 00:13:38,701
how could you face everyone at school?

178
00:13:39,961 --> 00:13:42,771
So let's all live together. Okay?

179
00:13:43,271 --> 00:13:45,771
And you kids need to convince Gyu Rim too.

180
00:13:46,371 --> 00:13:49,641
If I die like this, you'll regret it forever. Seriously.

181
00:13:49,711 --> 00:13:51,671
You're the one who abandoned us first, Dad.

182
00:13:53,081 --> 00:13:54,611
I did? When?

183
00:13:54,811 --> 00:13:56,351
If I had abandoned you,

184
00:13:56,411 --> 00:13:57,911
do you think you would've grown up so well?

185
00:13:57,981 --> 00:14:01,081
Gyu Rim raised us, not you.

186
00:14:01,681 --> 00:14:03,121
I raised you too, you know.

187
00:14:03,251 --> 00:14:06,661
I changed your dirty diapers and put you in your walker.

188
00:14:07,021 --> 00:14:09,261
In any case, I'm the one who brought you into this world, so...

189
00:14:09,331 --> 00:14:10,731
Then why did you?

190
00:14:11,491 --> 00:14:13,601
Why did you have us without asking first?

191
00:14:14,331 --> 00:14:15,471
You little brat.

192
00:14:16,371 --> 00:14:18,071
To the father who gave you the gift of life,

193
00:14:18,131 --> 00:14:19,601
you're asking why I had you?

194
00:14:20,001 --> 00:14:21,771
I had you out of love. Why?

195
00:14:21,901 --> 00:14:24,471
I was so in love with your mother that I had you.

196
00:14:24,811 --> 00:14:25,811
What are you going to do about it?

197
00:14:25,881 --> 00:14:27,511
You were a married man with a wife and kids.

198
00:14:27,581 --> 00:14:29,281
Why were you in love with another woman?

199
00:14:29,381 --> 00:14:30,851
Why?

200
00:14:30,911 --> 00:14:32,851
I told you, your mother seduced me.

201
00:14:32,851 --> 00:14:35,251
How is anyone supposed to resist a woman...

202
00:14:35,251 --> 00:14:36,621
who's determined to con them?

203
00:14:36,691 --> 00:14:38,761
Especially a man like me who's so full of love.

204
00:14:38,821 --> 00:14:40,121
If we hadn't been born,

205
00:14:40,191 --> 00:14:42,431
you wouldn't have divorced Gyu Rim's mom.

206
00:14:42,561 --> 00:14:43,831
If we had never been born,

207
00:14:44,131 --> 00:14:46,361
Gyu Rim wouldn't be having such a hard time now.

208
00:14:47,661 --> 00:14:50,331
Why? What is Gyu Rim saying?

209
00:14:51,171 --> 00:14:53,401
Is she telling you that her life is hard because of you?

210
00:14:54,171 --> 00:14:57,171
You know, Gyu Rim has been acting strange lately.

211
00:14:58,811 --> 00:14:59,941
You don't think Gyu Rim...

212
00:15:00,741 --> 00:15:03,851
has gotten involved in some weird cult, do you?

213
00:15:03,981 --> 00:15:05,381
Goodness.

214
00:15:07,421 --> 00:15:08,421
That little...

215
00:15:09,051 --> 00:15:11,451
- Unbelievable... - Hey, if Gyu Rim...

216
00:15:11,591 --> 00:15:14,561
gives you a hard time or is mean to you, you tell me.

217
00:15:14,891 --> 00:15:15,891
If even Gyu Rim starts acting up,

218
00:15:15,961 --> 00:15:17,091
the three of us will just live on our own.

219
00:15:20,161 --> 00:15:21,501
Dad, when are you going to grow up?

220
00:15:21,901 --> 00:15:24,071
Me? The day after tomorrow?

221
00:15:24,401 --> 00:15:26,301
Sure. The day after tomorrow.

222
00:15:26,801 --> 00:15:29,511
Whoever grows up first between you and Han Gyu Young...

223
00:15:29,641 --> 00:15:31,641
can have my entire fortune.

224
00:15:32,111 --> 00:15:33,111
And how much is your entire fortune?

225
00:15:33,181 --> 00:15:34,611
Whatever. Just go hang this up too.

226
00:15:34,711 --> 00:15:36,381
- Darn it. - How much is it?

227
00:15:37,011 --> 00:15:38,011
Hey.

228
00:15:40,221 --> 00:15:41,351
Such immature brats.

229
00:15:41,481 --> 00:15:44,491
(Lottery Retailer)

230
00:15:50,861 --> 00:15:54,501
(Lottery Retailer)

231
00:15:58,401 --> 00:15:59,441
Hello.

232
00:15:59,801 --> 00:16:01,801
Ten two-dollar scratch-off tickets, please.

233
00:16:09,051 --> 00:16:10,051
Please.

234
00:16:11,081 --> 00:16:12,081
That's not a winner!

235
00:16:17,351 --> 00:16:20,121
I don't even have to look to know it's not a winner.

236
00:16:21,821 --> 00:16:24,631
How can you expect to get lucky with an attitude like that?

237
00:16:26,731 --> 00:16:28,031
Please.

238
00:16:28,261 --> 00:16:30,231
Can't you just pretend you don't see me and walk on by?

239
00:16:30,331 --> 00:16:33,141
I was going to do just that, but whenever I see you,

240
00:16:33,201 --> 00:16:34,541
I wonder how to make a decent person out of you.

241
00:16:34,601 --> 00:16:36,111
I feel this overwhelming sense of responsibility.

242
00:16:36,311 --> 00:16:37,641
You're infuriating.

243
00:16:37,841 --> 00:16:39,981
You're the most infuriating person I know.

244
00:16:40,081 --> 00:16:41,081
Is that right?

245
00:16:41,841 --> 00:16:43,051
Well, of all the people I know,

246
00:16:43,111 --> 00:16:44,811
you're the most infuriating one to me too.

247
00:16:44,881 --> 00:16:47,921
At least we agree on that one thing, right?

248
00:16:48,381 --> 00:16:49,421
Darn it.

249
00:16:56,061 --> 00:16:57,231
When is she ever going to grow up?

250
00:17:18,281 --> 00:17:19,421
What are you looking at?

251
00:17:21,551 --> 00:17:22,691
That's Sung Wook, isn't it?

252
00:17:24,421 --> 00:17:25,421
No, it's not.

253
00:17:25,621 --> 00:17:26,821
Has that bastard lost his mind?

254
00:17:26,891 --> 00:17:28,421
His wedding is just around the corner!

255
00:17:30,661 --> 00:17:31,661
What are you going to do about it?

256
00:17:31,731 --> 00:17:33,131
I'm going to find him and beat him to a pulp.

257
00:17:33,301 --> 00:17:34,401
And why would you do that?

258
00:17:34,461 --> 00:17:36,701
Because that punk deserves to be beaten to death, doesn't he?

259
00:17:36,771 --> 00:17:37,971
What business is it of yours?

260
00:17:39,701 --> 00:17:43,071
I completely misjudged him.

261
00:17:43,441 --> 00:17:46,381
Just call off the wedding.

262
00:17:46,441 --> 00:17:48,341
What does someone else's business have to do with you?

263
00:17:48,411 --> 00:17:51,381
It's not someone else's business. Han Gyu Rim is like family to me,

264
00:17:52,621 --> 00:17:55,281
and this concerns her younger sister. Got it?

265
00:17:55,991 --> 00:17:59,121
If you even breathe a word of this, I swear I'll kill you.

266
00:17:59,191 --> 00:18:01,591
You're just going to let a bastard like that get away with it?

267
00:18:01,721 --> 00:18:03,591
Let it go. Just leave it alone!

268
00:18:04,291 --> 00:18:06,231
It's not like I'm marrying him for love anyway.

269
00:18:08,131 --> 00:18:09,131
You...

270
00:18:10,671 --> 00:18:12,401
What are you talking about?

271
00:18:14,741 --> 00:18:16,811
I am going through with this marriage no matter what.

272
00:18:17,271 --> 00:18:19,281
No matter what that bastard does,

273
00:18:20,211 --> 00:18:21,341
I'm still going to marry him.

274
00:18:22,751 --> 00:18:24,881
Don't you dare interfere. I swear I'll kill you.

275
00:18:39,861 --> 00:18:41,001
Oh, what should I do?

276
00:18:41,301 --> 00:18:45,471
I completely, by accident, knocked over the bucket of loaches.

277
00:18:45,901 --> 00:18:47,901
Since my back isn't what it used to be,

278
00:18:48,241 --> 00:18:50,211
you're going to have to pick them all up.

279
00:18:51,411 --> 00:18:53,641
- Me? - Well, who else is here?

280
00:18:54,341 --> 00:18:56,451
Hurry up and get them before the customers come.

281
00:18:59,551 --> 00:19:01,651
What, you can't do it?

282
00:19:02,621 --> 00:19:04,391
If you're angry and you don't like it,

283
00:19:04,391 --> 00:19:05,661
you can just quit.

284
00:19:07,191 --> 00:19:09,131
No. I'll get them all.

285
00:19:17,871 --> 00:19:20,401
By the way, I heard you've had an awakening?

286
00:19:20,501 --> 00:19:22,371
That from now on, you're not going...

287
00:19:22,371 --> 00:19:24,111
to do anything you don't want to, right?

288
00:19:24,311 --> 00:19:26,711
And that you're only going to think about yourself?

289
00:19:27,581 --> 00:19:30,581
I suppose that's why you turned down my Heung Sik.

290
00:19:31,251 --> 00:19:33,251
So why are you putting up with this now?

291
00:19:33,921 --> 00:19:36,251
Why are you doing all this unfair work...

292
00:19:36,251 --> 00:19:37,421
without a single complaint?

293
00:19:39,391 --> 00:19:43,091
What, are you collecting evidence to report me as an abusive boss?

294
00:19:43,191 --> 00:19:44,461
Is that it?

295
00:19:46,601 --> 00:19:48,001
Am I just a dog barking?

296
00:19:49,971 --> 00:19:51,771
It's because I don't think it's unfair.

297
00:19:52,971 --> 00:19:56,241
- What? - Strangely, I don't feel that...

298
00:19:56,241 --> 00:19:58,641
what you're asking me to do is unfair.

299
00:20:00,911 --> 00:20:02,481
That wasn't a mistake, you know.

300
00:20:02,951 --> 00:20:06,421
I know you're more scared of live loaches than anything.

301
00:20:06,851 --> 00:20:09,851
I did it on purpose to give you a hard time.

302
00:20:10,021 --> 00:20:11,291
Too bad for you!

303
00:20:16,231 --> 00:20:18,331
Gosh, you're a tough one.

304
00:20:18,691 --> 00:20:21,361
Fine. Let's see just how unfair I can be.

305
00:20:21,701 --> 00:20:26,241
We'll see how long you can take it.

306
00:20:27,341 --> 00:20:28,401
Oh, my goodness.

307
00:20:48,121 --> 00:20:49,591
Honey, are you okay?

308
00:20:52,601 --> 00:20:53,601
Yes.

309
00:20:56,701 --> 00:20:59,801
Why are you looking at me that way? Is there something on my face?

310
00:21:00,441 --> 00:21:01,671
Oh, honey, your...

311
00:21:02,471 --> 00:21:03,641
Is there something on my face?

312
00:21:05,641 --> 00:21:07,111
Oh my gosh. What happened to my face?

313
00:21:10,511 --> 00:21:11,551
I'm losing my mind.

314
00:21:12,181 --> 00:21:13,221
It's okay.

315
00:21:39,881 --> 00:21:40,881
Honey.

316
00:21:43,211 --> 00:21:45,681
Are you okay? Here, have some tea.

317
00:21:47,251 --> 00:21:48,251
I'm sorry.

318
00:21:49,051 --> 00:21:51,351
- You must have been startled by me. - No.

319
00:21:54,221 --> 00:21:55,891
I was lost in thought.

320
00:21:57,691 --> 00:21:59,801
I didn't even realise what I was doing.

321
00:22:02,471 --> 00:22:05,531
Can I know what you were thinking about?

322
00:22:09,841 --> 00:22:12,341
Or do I have to wait until you want to talk?

323
00:22:17,911 --> 00:22:20,581
You don't have to tell me. It's all right. I should get going.

324
00:22:21,681 --> 00:22:22,791
I'll tell you.

325
00:22:27,191 --> 00:22:28,921
I'll tell you everything.

326
00:22:31,591 --> 00:22:32,601
What is it?

327
00:22:38,401 --> 00:22:39,401
That girl...

328
00:22:41,941 --> 00:22:43,171
is my daughter.

329
00:22:46,211 --> 00:22:48,081
The one Mu Jin was seeing...

330
00:22:51,251 --> 00:22:52,621
That's Gyu Rim.

331
00:23:01,621 --> 00:23:02,691
That's why...

332
00:23:05,391 --> 00:23:07,761
That's why I was so against it.

333
00:23:11,131 --> 00:23:12,541
I'm sorry, honey.

334
00:23:13,641 --> 00:23:15,701
To you and to Seo Hyun.

335
00:23:17,571 --> 00:23:19,181
I'm so, so sorry.

336
00:23:35,291 --> 00:23:36,291
Mom.

337
00:23:42,871 --> 00:23:45,331
- Mom. - Oh, Seo Hyun.

338
00:23:51,341 --> 00:23:52,981
Mom, were you crying?

339
00:23:53,481 --> 00:23:54,711
No.

340
00:23:55,341 --> 00:23:56,951
It's just my allergies.

341
00:23:57,351 --> 00:23:58,951
Did Dad make you cry?

342
00:24:05,021 --> 00:24:07,091
Mom, can I talk to you for a second...

343
00:24:08,061 --> 00:24:10,691
Never mind. Dad, you should hear this too.

344
00:24:27,981 --> 00:24:29,881
I knew something was strange.

345
00:24:30,081 --> 00:24:31,951
You're not usually like this, Mom.

346
00:24:32,051 --> 00:24:33,951
I knew there had to be a reason...

347
00:24:33,951 --> 00:24:36,321
for the way you were so horrible to Mu Jin and opposed him,

348
00:24:36,391 --> 00:24:37,851
and it's been bothering me.

349
00:24:39,491 --> 00:24:42,631
I'm not one to beat around the bush, so I'm going to ask you directly.

350
00:24:45,231 --> 00:24:47,431
Is Mu Jin your son, Dad?

351
00:24:50,701 --> 00:24:51,771
Seo Hyun.

352
00:24:52,201 --> 00:24:53,701
If he's not, just say so.

353
00:24:54,201 --> 00:24:56,271
Is Mu Jin your son, Dad?

354
00:24:57,811 --> 00:24:58,971
What are you talking about?

355
00:24:59,481 --> 00:25:01,341
How could you say something so ridiculous?

356
00:25:01,581 --> 00:25:04,851
When I think about Dad and Mu Jin, they're so much alike.

357
00:25:05,011 --> 00:25:06,621
You have the same blood type.

358
00:25:06,681 --> 00:25:08,621
Your tastes in coffee and wine are ridiculously similar.

359
00:25:08,681 --> 00:25:10,291
You're both huge fans of Erik Satie,

360
00:25:10,551 --> 00:25:12,621
and you both suffer from pollen allergies in the spring,

361
00:25:12,791 --> 00:25:14,391
and you both catch colds all winter long.

362
00:25:14,461 --> 00:25:15,491
Even you both like soft rice...

363
00:25:15,561 --> 00:25:18,561
- and prefer to dip your food. - You're grasping at straws.

364
00:25:18,861 --> 00:25:20,401
How could you say that about your father?

365
00:25:20,861 --> 00:25:23,631
Don't you know what kind of man your father is?

366
00:25:24,201 --> 00:25:25,801
How could you say such a thing?

367
00:25:26,471 --> 00:25:27,801
Dad, explain yourself.

368
00:25:28,571 --> 00:25:29,811
Am I overreacting?

369
00:25:30,141 --> 00:25:32,881
Am I making a huge mistake by asking you this?

370
00:25:34,441 --> 00:25:35,781
Seo Hyun.

371
00:25:36,181 --> 00:25:37,481
It's not like that.

372
00:25:39,381 --> 00:25:40,651
Since I...

373
00:25:40,721 --> 00:25:42,351
was so against you and Mu Jin,

374
00:25:42,421 --> 00:25:44,421
I think you've become overly sensitive about this.

375
00:25:46,021 --> 00:25:47,361
I'll tell you everything.

376
00:25:48,521 --> 00:25:50,731
- I'll tell you everything... - That's right.

377
00:25:55,661 --> 00:25:56,671
It's true.

378
00:25:57,471 --> 00:25:58,801
Mu Jin is my son.

379
00:25:59,001 --> 00:26:00,001
Honey.

380
00:26:03,171 --> 00:26:04,541
He is my son...

381
00:26:05,041 --> 00:26:07,981
It's just that for various reasons,

382
00:26:08,041 --> 00:26:10,011
Chairman Hong has been raising him all this time.

383
00:26:12,611 --> 00:26:14,881
Seo Hyun, no. It's not like that.

384
00:26:16,851 --> 00:26:18,921
I was just so frustrated...

385
00:26:18,991 --> 00:26:20,861
that I said the first thing that came to mind.

386
00:26:21,561 --> 00:26:24,861
You're not supposed to take me so seriously.

387
00:26:25,731 --> 00:26:28,101
You should have yelled at me, asking what I take you for,

388
00:26:28,161 --> 00:26:30,001
and scolded me. That would have been the normal reaction.

389
00:26:30,831 --> 00:26:31,871
No. Listen to me.

390
00:26:32,531 --> 00:26:34,201
He's a child I had when I was immature,

391
00:26:34,201 --> 00:26:35,671
before I got married.

392
00:26:36,841 --> 00:26:38,241
And that child...

393
00:26:38,741 --> 00:26:40,681
was raised by Chairman Hong all this time,

394
00:26:41,081 --> 00:26:43,081
and I only found out about it recently myself.

395
00:26:43,181 --> 00:26:44,181
Honey.

396
00:26:44,951 --> 00:26:46,481
No. Seo Hyun, it's not like that.

397
00:26:46,551 --> 00:26:48,081
- I'm sorry, honey. - It's not like that.

398
00:26:48,081 --> 00:26:50,121
- I'm sorry I couldn't tell you. - Seo Hyun.

399
00:26:50,191 --> 00:26:54,361
I'll tell you everything, Seo Hyun. I'll explain everything.

400
00:26:54,421 --> 00:26:56,391
What is going on?

401
00:26:57,731 --> 00:27:00,161
Gosh, I guess I can't even make a joke around here.

402
00:27:00,801 --> 00:27:04,731
I can't even tell a joke. Seriously, what is this?

403
00:27:06,001 --> 00:27:07,001
Seo Hyun.

404
00:27:07,271 --> 00:27:09,041
- Seo Hyun. - Honey...

405
00:27:09,101 --> 00:27:10,111
Honey!

406
00:27:11,641 --> 00:27:13,881
Why are you telling such a ridiculous lie?

407
00:27:16,211 --> 00:27:17,281
Let's just go with that.

408
00:27:18,211 --> 00:27:20,021
Let's just say that Mu Jin is my son.

409
00:27:20,551 --> 00:27:21,751
So that...

410
00:27:21,881 --> 00:27:24,491
Seo Hyun and Mu Jin can't be together.

411
00:27:25,191 --> 00:27:27,321
They can't be together anyway, right?

412
00:27:27,461 --> 00:27:29,691
So what does the reason matter? Right?

413
00:27:30,031 --> 00:27:31,461
It's because of me.

414
00:27:32,031 --> 00:27:34,401
You can just tell her the truth, that it's because of me.

415
00:27:34,631 --> 00:27:37,131
Why are you taking all the blame?

416
00:27:38,971 --> 00:27:42,041
No. I'm going to tell Seo Hyun everything.

417
00:27:42,301 --> 00:27:43,871
And if you tell her the truth?

418
00:27:44,171 --> 00:27:46,341
Seo Hyun will never want to see you again.

419
00:27:48,641 --> 00:27:49,781
Are you okay with that?

420
00:27:50,381 --> 00:27:51,581
Because I'm not.

421
00:27:52,781 --> 00:27:54,551
I don't want my daughter, Seo Hyun,

422
00:27:55,121 --> 00:27:57,321
to lose her mother again.

423
00:27:58,651 --> 00:28:00,621
Think of how you raised her.

424
00:28:01,321 --> 00:28:03,231
Seo Hyun adores you.

425
00:28:03,461 --> 00:28:05,161
She likes you more than she likes me.

426
00:28:06,331 --> 00:28:07,601
But even so...

427
00:28:09,401 --> 00:28:10,771
Does this make any sense?

428
00:28:11,901 --> 00:28:14,801
To say Mu Jin is your son? Does that make any sense?

429
00:28:14,871 --> 00:28:16,041
Of course not.

430
00:28:16,041 --> 00:28:18,341
It has to be unbelievable for Seo Hyun to back down.

431
00:28:18,871 --> 00:28:20,681
You know what Seo Hyun is like.

432
00:28:20,841 --> 00:28:23,751
She only gives up when something defies all common sense.

433
00:28:23,811 --> 00:28:24,911
Honey.

434
00:28:25,451 --> 00:28:26,521
Yes, I know.

435
00:28:27,051 --> 00:28:28,951
I know how absurd this whole situation is, but...

436
00:28:29,621 --> 00:28:30,621
Honey,

437
00:28:31,321 --> 00:28:33,391
I'll handle this one way or another,

438
00:28:33,521 --> 00:28:35,521
so just do exactly as I say.

439
00:28:35,521 --> 00:28:37,161
Don't say a word,

440
00:28:37,461 --> 00:28:38,731
and just be quiet.

441
00:28:39,661 --> 00:28:40,661
Okay?

442
00:28:41,761 --> 00:28:42,761
All right?

443
00:28:44,201 --> 00:28:45,201
It will be fine.

444
00:28:49,071 --> 00:28:50,111
Hey, what?

445
00:28:52,771 --> 00:28:54,111
Hey, say that again.

446
00:28:54,781 --> 00:28:56,751
Whose son did you just say Mu Jin is?

447
00:28:57,851 --> 00:29:01,221
My son. We're going to say he's my son.

448
00:29:01,351 --> 00:29:02,481
Hear me out.

449
00:29:02,651 --> 00:29:03,651
Listen.

450
00:29:03,721 --> 00:29:05,591
Look, when I was young and foolish,

451
00:29:05,651 --> 00:29:08,021
I had a child out of wedlock.

452
00:29:08,421 --> 00:29:10,031
But since you wanted a son,

453
00:29:10,091 --> 00:29:12,491
you took that child in and raised him all this time.

454
00:29:13,131 --> 00:29:15,001
So that would mean I'm not his real mother?

455
00:29:15,961 --> 00:29:17,101
That would be correct.

456
00:29:17,571 --> 00:29:18,601
Hey.

457
00:29:19,271 --> 00:29:22,771
Why do we need a ridiculous story like that now?

458
00:29:23,371 --> 00:29:24,371
Why?

459
00:29:26,381 --> 00:29:27,781
Because it has to be this extreme...

460
00:29:27,781 --> 00:29:30,081
for Seo Hyun to break up with Mu Jin.

461
00:29:30,551 --> 00:29:33,281
Gosh, I said I hadn't had a good laugh in a while,

462
00:29:33,351 --> 00:29:36,791
so did you come to crack me up? It's really hilarious.

463
00:29:36,851 --> 00:29:38,421
Absolutely hilarious.

464
00:29:40,491 --> 00:29:43,161
- You owe me, remember? - What?

465
00:29:43,231 --> 00:29:44,231
Did you forget?

466
00:29:45,191 --> 00:29:46,631
Back in college, in the mountaineering club,

467
00:29:46,631 --> 00:29:48,201
when we went rock climbing,

468
00:29:48,261 --> 00:29:50,501
you almost fell to your death from a cliff, and I saved you.

469
00:29:51,171 --> 00:29:52,801
What did you tell me then?

470
00:29:53,041 --> 00:29:56,641
You said that one day, you'd get the chance to save me...

471
00:29:56,641 --> 00:29:58,611
and you'd repay your debt then.

472
00:29:58,771 --> 00:30:00,911
- You promised. - Are you dying?

473
00:30:01,381 --> 00:30:04,951
So, pay that debt back now. Okay?

474
00:30:05,181 --> 00:30:07,981
Okay, I know it's ridiculous and absurd. Let's just...

475
00:30:08,051 --> 00:30:11,151
get our story straight, at least for Seo Hyun.

476
00:30:11,221 --> 00:30:13,861
I know you want to separate Mu Jin and Seo Hyun,

477
00:30:13,961 --> 00:30:15,561
but still, how could you come up with something so insane?

478
00:30:15,621 --> 00:30:17,391
Even a grade-schooler would laugh at this.

479
00:30:17,461 --> 00:30:19,291
Fine, whatever. Laugh at me or blame me.

480
00:30:19,361 --> 00:30:21,401
I'll take it all. Just...

481
00:30:21,831 --> 00:30:23,871
Please just grant me this one favour?

482
00:30:23,931 --> 00:30:26,601
- No way, you jerk. - Hey.

483
00:30:27,171 --> 00:30:28,841
If you want to act like a madman, do it yourself.

484
00:30:28,901 --> 00:30:31,011
Why are you trying to drag me into your craziness?

485
00:30:31,071 --> 00:30:33,741
Hey, so that means I knew they were brother and sister,

486
00:30:33,811 --> 00:30:35,581
and I tried to marry them... No way...

487
00:30:35,841 --> 00:30:36,851
Hey.

488
00:30:37,251 --> 00:30:38,581
It's too disgusting to even say out loud.

489
00:30:38,651 --> 00:30:40,921
Are you out of your mind?

490
00:30:41,151 --> 00:30:42,281
Then what am I supposed to do?

491
00:30:42,351 --> 00:30:43,721
What, should I get on my knees again?

492
00:30:43,791 --> 00:30:46,191
- Get on my knees again? - What are you talking about?

493
00:30:46,251 --> 00:30:48,761
Hey. If you help me this time,

494
00:30:48,821 --> 00:30:50,561
you'll basically be saving my life...

495
00:30:50,631 --> 00:30:51,731
Yes, for the second time,

496
00:30:51,791 --> 00:30:54,761
and I swear I'll spend the rest of my life repaying you.

497
00:30:54,861 --> 00:30:56,301
So please, do this for me just this one time.

498
00:30:56,371 --> 00:30:58,531
Hey, fine, I'm sorry. Okay.

499
00:30:58,631 --> 00:31:00,741
I'm sorry you suddenly found out you're not his birth mother.

500
00:31:00,801 --> 00:31:02,601
Anyway, this whole situation is...

501
00:31:02,841 --> 00:31:04,271
So please. Hey.

502
00:31:04,541 --> 00:31:06,811
Ok Seon. Chairman Hong.

503
00:31:07,781 --> 00:31:09,111
Do you have any idea how desperate I am?

504
00:31:09,711 --> 00:31:10,781
Do you?

505
00:31:11,511 --> 00:31:13,051
Unbelievable...

506
00:31:15,721 --> 00:31:16,891
Come on.

507
00:31:17,021 --> 00:31:18,751
You must have misheard.

508
00:31:19,191 --> 00:31:22,591
Does that even make sense? I was just rambling.

509
00:31:24,931 --> 00:31:28,261
The Chairman's joke went too far.

510
00:31:29,561 --> 00:31:32,331
Check your phone. Your dad was just joking.

511
00:31:32,401 --> 00:31:33,671
I'm sure the Chairman sent you a text.

512
00:31:34,541 --> 00:31:36,371
I got a text a little while ago.

513
00:31:36,611 --> 00:31:39,511
He said he doesn't know how to ask for my forgiveness.

514
00:31:39,611 --> 00:31:40,681
So that means...

515
00:31:42,681 --> 00:31:45,211
So, it's true? Really?

516
00:31:47,921 --> 00:31:49,481
I should have just pretended I didn't know.

517
00:31:50,851 --> 00:31:52,921
I shouldn't have asked anything.

518
00:31:58,591 --> 00:32:00,731
I don't believe it. I can't believe it.

519
00:32:00,831 --> 00:32:02,461
How could the Chairman and Mu Jin's mother...

520
00:32:02,531 --> 00:32:04,331
do something so irresponsible and despicable...

521
00:32:06,541 --> 00:32:08,941
This is absurd. How is this even possible?

522
00:32:10,441 --> 00:32:12,241
I should've just had a baby with him.

523
00:32:12,311 --> 00:32:13,311
Hey.

524
00:32:13,481 --> 00:32:14,781
What kind of crazy thing is that to say?

525
00:32:18,551 --> 00:32:19,781
How far did you two go?

526
00:32:20,051 --> 00:32:22,581
- Did you even kiss? - We couldn't meet to do anything.

527
00:32:22,881 --> 00:32:25,721
My mom never even let the two of us meet alone.

528
00:32:26,861 --> 00:32:28,761
Even if you had, you know Mu Jin...

529
00:32:28,891 --> 00:32:30,761
If he's not truly in love with a woman,

530
00:32:30,831 --> 00:32:32,431
he's the type who can't even properly hold her hand...

531
00:32:32,761 --> 00:32:33,831
Gosh...

532
00:32:38,571 --> 00:32:39,601
Does Mu Jin know?

533
00:32:41,141 --> 00:32:45,341
- Have you told Mu Jin? - Darn it.

534
00:32:48,241 --> 00:32:49,641
Seriously.

535
00:32:52,881 --> 00:32:54,981
(Damga Charcoal Grill)

536
00:33:11,631 --> 00:33:12,631
Chairman.

537
00:33:13,901 --> 00:33:14,901
Hey.

538
00:33:15,771 --> 00:33:16,771
Sit down.

539
00:33:18,671 --> 00:33:20,481
You've been drinking a lot lately.

540
00:33:20,981 --> 00:33:22,411
Even drinking during the day.

541
00:33:22,481 --> 00:33:23,581
(Damga Charcoal Grill)

542
00:33:25,881 --> 00:33:27,681
By any chance, have you heard from Seo Hyun?

543
00:33:28,451 --> 00:33:29,451
No.

544
00:33:30,091 --> 00:33:31,251
Is something wrong?

545
00:33:33,121 --> 00:33:35,121
And no calls to your mother either?

546
00:33:36,991 --> 00:33:38,091
What's going on?

547
00:33:41,231 --> 00:33:42,301
Want a drink?

548
00:33:42,901 --> 00:33:43,901
No.

549
00:33:46,131 --> 00:33:47,341
I'll have just one glass.

550
00:33:48,271 --> 00:33:50,071
Excuse me, can we get another glass over here?

551
00:33:50,071 --> 00:33:51,341
Yes, right away.

552
00:33:53,611 --> 00:33:54,611
Mu Jin.

553
00:33:57,711 --> 00:33:59,651
By any chance,

554
00:34:01,981 --> 00:34:04,991
was the person you used to date Han Gyu Rim?

555
00:34:11,031 --> 00:34:12,031
So it's true.

556
00:34:13,301 --> 00:34:14,761
It was Han Gyu Rim, wasn't it?

557
00:34:18,101 --> 00:34:20,001
(Damga Charcoal Grill)

558
00:34:28,511 --> 00:34:30,611
Why are you suddenly asking about Gyu Rim?

559
00:34:32,181 --> 00:34:33,581
Han Gyu Rim is...

560
00:34:35,151 --> 00:34:37,151
Yoon Hee's eldest daughter, whom Yoon Hee left behind...

561
00:34:37,621 --> 00:34:38,951
when she divorced.

562
00:34:40,021 --> 00:34:41,021
What?

563
00:34:43,631 --> 00:34:44,731
Chairman.

564
00:34:45,831 --> 00:34:49,231
That's why Yoon Hee was so against you and Seo Hyun.

565
00:34:54,371 --> 00:34:55,541
Seo Hyun still doesn't know.

566
00:34:57,441 --> 00:34:58,771
I plan to keep it that way.

567
00:35:00,441 --> 00:35:01,441
So...

568
00:35:03,911 --> 00:35:05,081
end it...

569
00:35:06,211 --> 00:35:07,351
between you and Seo Hyun.

570
00:35:22,131 --> 00:35:23,471
I had to tell Seo Hyun...

571
00:35:24,271 --> 00:35:27,271
a ridiculous reason to why the two of you couldn't be together.

572
00:35:29,471 --> 00:35:30,971
That's the only way she'll give up.

573
00:35:32,911 --> 00:35:35,711
What I said was...

574
00:35:37,751 --> 00:35:39,851
No, never mind. This is just too absurd.

575
00:35:40,621 --> 00:35:44,551
Whatever Seo Hyun says, don't say anything to her.

576
00:35:45,991 --> 00:35:49,931
Just stay away from her.

577
00:35:51,431 --> 00:35:52,431
Do you understand?

578
00:35:56,101 --> 00:35:57,101
My head is spinning.

579
00:35:59,801 --> 00:36:01,201
I'm sorry for confusing you.

580
00:36:07,311 --> 00:36:08,681
Han Gyu Rim is...

581
00:36:09,211 --> 00:36:11,381
Yoon Hee's eldest daughter, whom Yoon Hee left behind...

582
00:36:11,711 --> 00:36:13,011
when she divorced.

583
00:36:14,621 --> 00:36:17,151
Why did you date her if you were just going to end it like this?

584
00:36:18,151 --> 00:36:20,321
Why date her if you couldn't take responsibility?

585
00:36:21,621 --> 00:36:24,161
Why did you date her if you couldn't even protect her?

586
00:36:29,131 --> 00:36:31,201
As for me, maybe it's because I'm a mother to a daughter,

587
00:36:32,271 --> 00:36:34,341
but I can't stop thinking about that other girl.

588
00:36:35,371 --> 00:36:36,741
But she was treated...

589
00:36:38,241 --> 00:36:39,941
like a gold digger by your family.

590
00:36:42,241 --> 00:36:44,381
After enduring all that pain and humiliation,

591
00:36:46,981 --> 00:36:48,621
I can't imagine how she must have felt when she left you.

592
00:37:06,941 --> 00:37:09,241
Oh my, this is so good.

593
00:37:11,741 --> 00:37:13,071
This is so delicious...

594
00:37:13,941 --> 00:37:15,011
But that rotten woman...

595
00:37:16,711 --> 00:37:17,851
Who was that lady?

596
00:37:18,811 --> 00:37:20,181
Are you asking me?

597
00:37:21,121 --> 00:37:22,581
Well, who else would I be asking?

598
00:37:22,651 --> 00:37:25,851
Am I asking these dried greens? Am I asking this radish kimchi?

599
00:37:28,361 --> 00:37:29,361
Who?

600
00:37:29,461 --> 00:37:32,691
- Who are you talking about? - You know, her.

601
00:37:32,861 --> 00:37:35,731
The one wearing sunglasses just to buy side dishes,

602
00:37:35,801 --> 00:37:38,831
looking like a spy. That obnoxious woman.

603
00:37:39,801 --> 00:37:41,971
She was asking if you were Han Gyu Rim.

604
00:37:42,441 --> 00:37:43,441
So who was she?

605
00:37:43,671 --> 00:37:46,141
- She asked for me by name? - Yes.

606
00:37:46,841 --> 00:37:48,311
I don't think I know her.

607
00:37:48,511 --> 00:37:49,581
What do you mean, you don't know?

608
00:37:50,351 --> 00:37:53,781
Now I see. You sent her, didn't you?

609
00:37:54,351 --> 00:37:56,951
To drive me crazy, right?

610
00:37:57,091 --> 00:37:59,451
You sent her to get your revenge for you, right?

611
00:38:00,461 --> 00:38:02,091
I did no such thing.

612
00:38:02,361 --> 00:38:03,661
It's true, isn't it?

613
00:38:04,231 --> 00:38:06,291
There's a strange resemblance.

614
00:38:06,761 --> 00:38:08,061
You two definitely know each other.

615
00:38:08,861 --> 00:38:10,071
She must be your relative.

616
00:38:10,371 --> 00:38:14,301
- I don't have any relatives, Ma'am. - Don't even try to deny it.

617
00:38:14,901 --> 00:38:16,101
I can tell just by looking.

618
00:38:16,171 --> 00:38:17,511
(Gyeol's Teacher)

619
00:38:18,441 --> 00:38:21,241
I'm getting a call from Gyeol's teacher.

620
00:38:21,311 --> 00:38:22,311
I need to take this.

621
00:38:22,381 --> 00:38:23,711
It must be that awful woman.

622
00:38:24,251 --> 00:38:27,051
Tell her to show her face to me again.

623
00:38:27,581 --> 00:38:29,151
I'll wrap some rocks in kimchi...

624
00:38:29,151 --> 00:38:30,751
and shove her head in a pickling jar.

625
00:38:32,021 --> 00:38:35,621
- Hello? - Hello. This is Gyeol's teacher.

626
00:38:36,261 --> 00:38:38,661
Has Gyeol made it home yet?

627
00:38:38,731 --> 00:38:41,501
I'm at work right now.

628
00:38:42,031 --> 00:38:43,471
Is something wrong with Gyeol?

629
00:38:45,771 --> 00:38:46,971
Well,

630
00:38:47,141 --> 00:38:51,511
I'm not sure how to say this, but...

631
00:38:52,311 --> 00:38:54,641
Please, just tell me.

632
00:38:56,281 --> 00:38:57,351
Did Gyeol...

633
00:38:58,051 --> 00:39:01,521
get into some kind of trouble at school?

634
00:39:02,021 --> 00:39:03,381
No, it's not that.

635
00:39:07,691 --> 00:39:10,331
The kids were watching a science video,

636
00:39:12,261 --> 00:39:14,301
and they started talking about blood types.

637
00:39:15,661 --> 00:39:16,931
According to Gyeol,

638
00:39:18,471 --> 00:39:20,901
your blood type is Type O,

639
00:39:23,841 --> 00:39:27,511
and he said his is Type AB.

640
00:39:29,481 --> 00:39:30,481
Is that correct?

641
00:39:31,981 --> 00:39:32,981
Yes, that's right.

642
00:39:34,381 --> 00:39:35,381
Why do you ask?

643
00:39:38,721 --> 00:39:40,591
A mother with Type O blood...

644
00:39:41,861 --> 00:39:44,491
can't have a child with Type AB blood...

645
00:39:46,661 --> 00:39:48,561
regardless of the father's blood type.

646
00:39:52,631 --> 00:39:54,971
I know I'm overstepping,

647
00:39:56,041 --> 00:39:58,171
but to take better care of Gyeol,

648
00:39:58,741 --> 00:40:02,341
it's very helpful to have the correct information about him.

649
00:40:04,151 --> 00:40:07,421
Could you please be honest with me?

650
00:40:09,981 --> 00:40:10,991
Gyeol is...

651
00:40:13,321 --> 00:40:14,461
my son.

652
00:40:15,121 --> 00:40:16,691
Of course. I know.

653
00:40:17,331 --> 00:40:20,231
I can tell from his school journal how much you love him.

654
00:40:21,831 --> 00:40:25,171
Of all the parents in my class, you're by far the best.

655
00:40:25,271 --> 00:40:26,701
I know that better than anyone.

656
00:40:28,771 --> 00:40:31,541
Did the other kids tease him a lot?

657
00:40:35,981 --> 00:40:36,981
I'm so sorry.

658
00:40:38,781 --> 00:40:40,421
It was during recess, so I didn't realise...

659
00:40:43,121 --> 00:40:44,351
I'm truly sorry.

660
00:40:50,121 --> 00:40:51,131
No, it's not your fault.

661
00:40:53,801 --> 00:40:54,801
It's my fault.

662
00:40:56,761 --> 00:40:57,931
It's all my fault.

663
00:41:06,341 --> 00:41:09,881
(Son)

664
00:41:18,851 --> 00:41:20,891
The person you are calling is unavailable...

665
00:41:21,321 --> 00:41:22,591
Gyeol isn't picking up?

666
00:41:26,031 --> 00:41:27,031
What if Gyeol...

667
00:41:28,631 --> 00:41:30,431
is really upset?

668
00:41:32,801 --> 00:41:34,671
He must be so shaken up.

669
00:41:38,911 --> 00:41:39,941
What should I do?

670
00:41:41,411 --> 00:41:42,511
My poor baby.

671
00:42:02,101 --> 00:42:03,101
Open...

672
00:42:09,271 --> 00:42:10,911
Right. Don't open it.

673
00:42:11,911 --> 00:42:13,781
What could you possibly say today?

674
00:42:18,051 --> 00:42:19,711
There's a 100 percent chance you'll cause trouble today,

675
00:42:19,781 --> 00:42:21,821
so don't even think about coming near the restaurant, got it?

676
00:42:22,121 --> 00:42:23,951
Go home, take the day off, and don't come in tomorrow either.

677
00:42:29,891 --> 00:42:31,491
Seo Hyun asked you not to contact her...

678
00:42:31,561 --> 00:42:32,891
until she's sorted things out.

679
00:42:59,451 --> 00:43:00,461
Gyeol.

680
00:43:03,521 --> 00:43:04,531
What happened to your face?

681
00:43:05,191 --> 00:43:06,191
Have you been crying?

682
00:43:11,501 --> 00:43:12,671
What's wrong?

683
00:43:15,941 --> 00:43:17,071
What's going on?

684
00:43:38,731 --> 00:43:39,731
All done?

685
00:43:40,461 --> 00:43:42,401
It's okay. I can do it.

686
00:43:49,641 --> 00:43:50,711
Do you want some warm milk?

687
00:43:50,911 --> 00:43:54,081
No. Cold milk, please. With a ton of ice in it.

688
00:44:07,961 --> 00:44:08,991
Have warm milk.

689
00:44:09,361 --> 00:44:11,731
Cold milk can give you a stomachache.

690
00:44:11,991 --> 00:44:12,991
Okay.

691
00:44:16,061 --> 00:44:17,501
Should I get you anything else?

692
00:44:21,671 --> 00:44:25,441
I know we already said our goodbyes, so I'm sorry for coming back.

693
00:44:27,311 --> 00:44:28,311
Don't be sorry.

694
00:44:29,341 --> 00:44:30,341
It's okay.

695
00:44:31,011 --> 00:44:32,551
I really missed you too.

696
00:44:34,081 --> 00:44:37,851
Of all the people I know, you're the smartest.

697
00:44:39,291 --> 00:44:41,521
My aunt Gyu Young is smart too,

698
00:44:42,191 --> 00:44:44,031
but she's such a jerk...

699
00:44:44,361 --> 00:44:46,631
that I can't talk to her about my problems.

700
00:44:47,761 --> 00:44:49,161
Well, you made the right choice.

701
00:44:50,631 --> 00:44:52,731
So, can I ask what you're worried about?

702
00:45:06,251 --> 00:45:08,021
(Possible Blood Types Based on Parents)

703
00:45:08,121 --> 00:45:09,121
What's this?

704
00:45:09,881 --> 00:45:11,891
A chart of possible blood types from parents.

705
00:45:12,791 --> 00:45:13,891
I can see that.

706
00:45:14,491 --> 00:45:16,991
- So why are you looking at this? - My mom is Type O,

707
00:45:17,061 --> 00:45:18,461
but I'm Type AB.

708
00:45:22,331 --> 00:45:23,331
See?

709
00:45:23,971 --> 00:45:25,671
You get it, don't you?

710
00:45:26,231 --> 00:45:29,241
You can tell right away that it's weird.

711
00:45:32,511 --> 00:45:33,981
Are you sure you're not mistaken about something?

712
00:45:36,041 --> 00:45:37,751
I know for a fact your mom is Type O.

713
00:45:39,481 --> 00:45:41,051
Are you positive that you're Type AB?

714
00:45:41,651 --> 00:45:42,781
I'm positive.

715
00:45:46,021 --> 00:45:48,961
A lot of people are mistaken about their own blood type.

716
00:45:49,791 --> 00:45:52,091
Let's go to a clinic nearby and check again with me.

717
00:45:52,231 --> 00:45:56,501
But what if we check again, and I'm still Type AB?

718
00:45:56,831 --> 00:45:59,701
Then that means I'm not really my mom's son, right?

719
00:46:04,341 --> 00:46:06,441
First, let's go meet your mom and talk to her...

720
00:46:06,511 --> 00:46:09,581
No. I don't want to see my mom.

721
00:46:23,361 --> 00:46:26,031
- What is it? - I'm going to go wash my face.

722
00:46:39,241 --> 00:46:40,611
(Mom)

723
00:46:47,481 --> 00:46:48,921
Gyeol, where are you?

724
00:46:49,551 --> 00:46:51,451
Why aren't you answering my calls?

725
00:46:53,291 --> 00:46:54,491
This is Kim Mu Jin.

726
00:46:55,961 --> 00:46:58,391
Why are you answering Gyeol's phone?

727
00:46:59,291 --> 00:47:00,831
I'm with Gyeol right now.

728
00:47:02,361 --> 00:47:03,761
He came to see me.

729
00:47:06,171 --> 00:47:07,171
Where are you?

730
00:47:07,771 --> 00:47:09,141
I'll go there now.

731
00:47:12,711 --> 00:47:15,381
I don't think now is a good time. Maybe in a little while.

732
00:47:16,881 --> 00:47:17,881
Well...

733
00:47:19,381 --> 00:47:21,651
Gyeol seems to be a little shaken up.

734
00:47:23,651 --> 00:47:25,791
He doesn't seem to want to see you right now.

735
00:47:29,361 --> 00:47:31,731
Try not to worry too much and wait for me.

736
00:47:31,791 --> 00:47:34,461
I'll calm him down and bring him to you.

737
00:47:59,551 --> 00:48:01,761
(Ji Yeol's Wife)

738
00:48:08,361 --> 00:48:11,401
I just got back from the hospital with Ji Yeol.

739
00:48:12,501 --> 00:48:13,931
The doctor says it looks like...

740
00:48:15,141 --> 00:48:17,441
he's going to need another surgery.

741
00:48:19,641 --> 00:48:21,781
Ji Yeol doesn't know I'm calling you.

742
00:48:22,511 --> 00:48:24,681
He told me absolutely not to call you.

743
00:48:26,481 --> 00:48:28,321
We don't have anywhere to get the money from,

744
00:48:29,081 --> 00:48:30,991
so I called because I felt so helpless.

745
00:48:32,321 --> 00:48:33,321
Okay.

746
00:48:35,091 --> 00:48:36,091
You did the right thing.

747
00:48:37,091 --> 00:48:38,431
When you get the estimate for the surgery,

748
00:48:39,731 --> 00:48:40,731
let me know.

749
00:48:41,231 --> 00:48:42,231
I'm sorry.

750
00:48:43,031 --> 00:48:44,031
I know you're going through a lot too,

751
00:48:44,101 --> 00:48:45,571
and all I ever do is ask you for money.

752
00:48:48,171 --> 00:48:51,571
But this is all your fault, isn't it?

753
00:48:52,671 --> 00:48:55,941
So I hope you don't think we're being too shameless.

754
00:49:34,521 --> 00:49:35,521
What is this?

755
00:49:35,581 --> 00:49:36,981
The key to a car I've only driven once.

756
00:49:37,491 --> 00:49:38,491
Just take it.

757
00:49:41,661 --> 00:49:44,361
Do you have any idea how hard it was to track you down?

758
00:49:44,861 --> 00:49:46,731
I waited in the parking garage for an hour.

759
00:49:48,031 --> 00:49:49,531
Why don't you cut the crap and get lost?

760
00:49:53,671 --> 00:49:55,901
Even without that one, I have a third car.

761
00:49:56,241 --> 00:49:57,771
Just think of it as a gift.

762
00:49:59,941 --> 00:50:03,141
Yoon Gi told me Han Gyu Oh is crazy about money.

763
00:50:04,211 --> 00:50:05,381
Was he wrong?

764
00:50:08,621 --> 00:50:11,591
Yoon Gi said Han Gyu Oh would sell his soul for money.

765
00:50:11,821 --> 00:50:13,291
Was he lying to me?

766
00:50:24,371 --> 00:50:26,631
I assume you're worried about Hee Na and Su Chan,

767
00:50:26,701 --> 00:50:29,141
but who cares about friendship or love?

768
00:50:29,671 --> 00:50:31,371
In the end, it's all about money.

769
00:50:31,541 --> 00:50:33,541
People betray and scam each other for money.

770
00:50:33,711 --> 00:50:34,711
That's just how it is.

771
00:50:43,851 --> 00:50:45,351
Are you really that rich?

772
00:50:46,721 --> 00:50:48,321
Yes, I'm loaded.

773
00:50:48,961 --> 00:50:51,061
I don't just have a lot. I have a ton.

774
00:50:51,161 --> 00:50:52,761
My family is unbelievably wealthy.

775
00:50:57,331 --> 00:50:58,331
You want to sleep with me?

776
00:51:00,031 --> 00:51:01,471
What?

777
00:51:01,771 --> 00:51:03,671
Pay me, then. I'll sleep with you.

778
00:51:04,241 --> 00:51:06,011
But I'm expensive.

779
00:51:07,341 --> 00:51:09,981
- Hey, Han Gyu Oh. - I don't take cars or cards.

780
00:51:10,081 --> 00:51:11,451
If you're interested, bring cash.

781
00:51:11,511 --> 00:51:12,511
An insane amount.

782
00:51:12,881 --> 00:51:13,881
Enough...

783
00:51:14,781 --> 00:51:16,181
to make me want to sell my soul.

784
00:51:22,521 --> 00:51:23,521
Seriously.

785
00:51:37,911 --> 00:51:39,471
Darn it.

786
00:51:52,751 --> 00:51:53,751
Kwon Hee Na.

787
00:51:54,561 --> 00:51:55,691
This is Han Gyu Oh.

788
00:51:56,521 --> 00:51:57,521
Let's meet just once.

789
00:51:58,591 --> 00:51:59,591
Just one time.

790
00:52:00,431 --> 00:52:01,501
(Gigolo)

791
00:52:13,741 --> 00:52:14,741
I won't ask for more.

792
00:52:15,141 --> 00:52:16,781
Just give me one hour of your time.

793
00:52:19,911 --> 00:52:21,621
(Gigolo)

794
00:52:22,451 --> 00:52:23,651
(Block Contact)

795
00:52:23,651 --> 00:52:24,691
(Block)

796
00:52:30,691 --> 00:52:33,991
(Kwon Hee Na)

797
00:52:45,941 --> 00:52:47,171
(Suragan Side Dishes)

798
00:52:47,311 --> 00:52:48,841
According to Gyeol,

799
00:52:49,241 --> 00:52:51,511
your blood type is Type O,

800
00:52:52,051 --> 00:52:55,451
and he said his is Type AB.

801
00:52:56,921 --> 00:52:59,221
A mother with Type O blood...

802
00:52:59,721 --> 00:53:02,791
can't have a child with Type AB blood.

803
00:53:06,861 --> 00:53:09,131
Gyeol seems to be a little shaken up.

804
00:53:10,731 --> 00:53:12,971
He doesn't seem to want to see you right now.

805
00:53:34,691 --> 00:53:36,591
How is this product doing?

806
00:53:37,591 --> 00:53:38,891
It's selling well.

807
00:53:39,491 --> 00:53:41,761
People are golfing a lot these days.

808
00:53:43,861 --> 00:53:46,301
This was designed by Manager Kim, wasn't it?

809
00:53:46,901 --> 00:53:48,071
These days...

810
00:53:53,311 --> 00:53:55,741
- The colours turned out great. - They're really perfect.

811
00:53:59,111 --> 00:54:00,111
Is she...

812
00:54:00,581 --> 00:54:01,951
Is she crying?

813
00:54:03,921 --> 00:54:04,921
Oh no.

814
00:54:25,941 --> 00:54:29,111
(Chairman Jang Hoon Tae)

815
00:54:44,731 --> 00:54:46,031
That bastard.

816
00:55:22,361 --> 00:55:23,661
Gosh, your lips are bright red.

817
00:55:26,001 --> 00:55:28,171
I wore this lipstick because you like it.

818
00:55:28,741 --> 00:55:29,841
Is it too sexy?

819
00:55:32,171 --> 00:55:34,241
Yes, it's darn sexy.

820
00:55:36,141 --> 00:55:37,181
By the way...

821
00:55:37,441 --> 00:55:40,451
Can't we just go register our marriage this week?

822
00:55:41,181 --> 00:55:43,181
What's the rush? We can do it after the wedding.

823
00:55:43,681 --> 00:55:45,791
I just want it in writing that you're mine...

824
00:55:45,791 --> 00:55:47,451
as soon as possible.

825
00:55:48,061 --> 00:55:51,861
Since when did Han Gyu Young get so hung up on a piece of paper?

826
00:55:51,961 --> 00:55:55,101
That's right. I love making things official on paper.

827
00:55:56,161 --> 00:55:57,831
I'm hungry. Is the food coming soon?

828
00:55:58,871 --> 00:56:01,471
- Heung Sik is coming. - Who? Jo Heung Sik?

829
00:56:02,101 --> 00:56:04,541
What? Why is he coming?

830
00:56:05,011 --> 00:56:07,211
He called earlier when you went to the restroom,

831
00:56:07,271 --> 00:56:09,711
so I told him to come over. He happened to be nearby.

832
00:56:10,081 --> 00:56:11,781
Without even asking me?

833
00:56:12,011 --> 00:56:14,251
How could he be so clueless and crash our date?

834
00:56:14,851 --> 00:56:15,851
Darn it.

835
00:56:16,581 --> 00:56:17,581
Sung Wook.

836
00:56:18,121 --> 00:56:19,121
Hey.

837
00:56:23,121 --> 00:56:24,861
It's been a while, Gyu Young.

838
00:56:25,191 --> 00:56:27,791
Hi. Have you been well?

839
00:56:28,201 --> 00:56:29,201
Yes.

840
00:56:30,061 --> 00:56:33,731
Since you two are on a date, I hope I'm not intruding.

841
00:56:34,171 --> 00:56:35,171
We're not on a date.

842
00:56:35,241 --> 00:56:36,701
We were just hungry and came to get something to eat.

843
00:56:37,741 --> 00:56:38,871
Have you eaten?

844
00:56:39,071 --> 00:56:40,071
No.

845
00:56:41,341 --> 00:56:42,541
My meal...

846
00:56:43,041 --> 00:56:44,041
is right here.

847
00:56:49,621 --> 00:56:53,351
- Am I your meal? - Yes, you're my meal today.

848
00:56:54,491 --> 00:56:55,721
Let's all sit down first.

849
00:56:56,191 --> 00:56:58,191
- Okay. - But, Heung Sik.

850
00:56:58,931 --> 00:57:00,531
What do you mean, I'm your meal?

851
00:57:01,431 --> 00:57:02,801
You take a guess.

852
00:57:04,831 --> 00:57:05,831
What could it be?

853
00:57:07,031 --> 00:57:08,301
What kind of meal am I?

854
00:57:09,601 --> 00:57:11,441
Wait...

855
00:57:12,311 --> 00:57:13,471
A happy meal?

856
00:57:19,981 --> 00:57:21,251
Honey, you have something on your glass.

857
00:57:23,021 --> 00:57:24,021
Oh, my...

858
00:57:24,821 --> 00:57:27,591
- Hey! - Oh, honey. I'm so sorry.

859
00:57:28,091 --> 00:57:30,891
Seriously? Darn it.

860
00:57:43,071 --> 00:57:44,441
Be careful.

861
00:57:44,711 --> 00:57:46,941
It was so obvious you spilled that wine on purpose.

862
00:57:47,941 --> 00:57:51,251
And you should try a new routine. Didn't you spill wine last time too?

863
00:57:51,381 --> 00:57:52,581
I told you I would kill you.

864
00:57:52,911 --> 00:57:54,781
I told you I'd kill you if you tried to ruin my marriage.

865
00:57:54,851 --> 00:57:55,851
Go ahead. Kill me.

866
00:57:56,781 --> 00:57:58,191
If I didn't know about it, fine.

867
00:57:58,251 --> 00:58:00,791
But now that I do, I can't pretend I don't.

868
00:58:02,421 --> 00:58:03,921
If Gyu Rim finds out,

869
00:58:03,991 --> 00:58:06,761
she'll break your legs to stop this marriage.

870
00:58:06,831 --> 00:58:08,961
That darn Han Gyu Rim.

871
00:58:09,801 --> 00:58:11,901
The moment I get married, she will be a complete stranger to me.

872
00:58:12,301 --> 00:58:14,201
Whether I use a robot vacuum to do the dishes...

873
00:58:14,271 --> 00:58:17,801
or fry eggs with Omega-3s, she has no say in my life,

874
00:58:17,871 --> 00:58:19,611
and she has agreed not to from now on.

875
00:58:21,311 --> 00:58:22,641
Have you ever heard of cutting someone off?

876
00:58:23,641 --> 00:58:26,951
Oh, for goodness' sake. You're so dense.

877
00:58:27,611 --> 00:58:29,951
You act so smart all the time.

878
00:58:30,421 --> 00:58:33,491
Why are you so set on a marriage that's bound to make you miserable?

879
00:58:33,991 --> 00:58:37,061
My standard for misery isn't love. It's money.

880
00:58:37,561 --> 00:58:38,561
Got it?

881
00:58:41,131 --> 00:58:44,231
How much is it? How much money would it take?

882
00:58:44,301 --> 00:58:45,801
I'll lend you the money, interest-free.

883
00:58:46,271 --> 00:58:47,271
What are you talking about?

884
00:58:48,901 --> 00:58:50,241
Get out of here before Sung Wook comes back.

885
00:58:50,441 --> 00:58:52,811
Unless you're going to live my life for me, get lost!

886
00:58:57,681 --> 00:58:58,711
Now that I've drawn my sword,

887
00:58:58,711 --> 00:59:00,651
I have to at least slice a radish, right?

888
00:59:02,321 --> 00:59:05,391
I'll just give him one flick on the forehead and go.

889
00:59:05,921 --> 00:59:07,791
- All right? - Mister.

890
00:59:10,321 --> 00:59:12,991
Darn it! Honestly...

891
00:59:15,801 --> 00:59:18,201
Where did that punk go?

892
00:59:30,781 --> 00:59:32,711
You crazy bastard.

893
00:59:32,951 --> 00:59:34,511
Hey, you punk!

894
00:59:44,961 --> 00:59:46,031
My tooth...

895
00:59:47,991 --> 00:59:49,261
My tooth...

896
00:59:52,471 --> 00:59:53,571
My tooth...

897
00:59:54,671 --> 00:59:58,871
- My tooth fell out. - Are you even human?

898
00:59:59,041 --> 01:00:00,671
You're a worthless animal, aren't you?

899
01:00:01,481 --> 01:00:02,711
That hurts...

900
01:00:02,741 --> 01:00:06,181
- You're killing me. - Honey!

901
01:00:06,411 --> 01:00:10,181
Honey! Save me.

902
01:00:17,391 --> 01:00:20,231
My tooth. Where's my tooth?

903
01:00:20,361 --> 01:00:23,161
My tooth.

904
01:00:25,071 --> 01:00:26,071
Jo Heung Sik.

905
01:00:28,871 --> 01:00:33,171
(Suragan Side Dishes)

906
01:00:55,901 --> 01:00:57,001
So...

907
01:00:58,271 --> 01:00:59,871
Are you feeling a little better now?

908
01:01:05,441 --> 01:01:06,771
Is there anything you want to eat?

909
01:01:11,711 --> 01:01:14,181
Then who's my mom?

910
01:01:14,781 --> 01:01:17,221
And who's my dad?

911
01:01:21,291 --> 01:01:26,031
Did my mom find me under a bridge?

912
01:01:28,831 --> 01:01:31,831
Where's the bridge she found me under?

913
01:01:34,071 --> 01:01:35,271
Gyeol.

914
01:01:36,371 --> 01:01:38,411
If you know where that bridge is,

915
01:01:39,041 --> 01:01:41,041
please take me there.

916
01:01:58,121 --> 01:01:59,861
Here, drink some water.

917
01:02:00,691 --> 01:02:02,431
If you keep crying, you'll get dehydrated.

918
01:02:10,801 --> 01:02:11,811
Good.

919
01:02:49,611 --> 01:02:51,811
I hear you're with Han Gyeol.

920
01:02:52,081 --> 01:02:54,281
Gyu Rim is asking you to call her cell phone.

921
01:02:54,781 --> 01:02:56,951
I'll listen to what the latest mess is when we meet.

922
01:02:57,281 --> 01:02:58,991
I'm sending Gyu Rim's number too.

923
01:03:10,961 --> 01:03:11,971
Hello?

924
01:03:12,571 --> 01:03:13,571
This is Kim Mu Jin.

925
01:03:14,471 --> 01:03:16,401
Are you with Gyeol right now?

926
01:03:17,041 --> 01:03:18,041
I'm sorry.

927
01:03:18,871 --> 01:03:22,011
I knew you'd be worried, but I wasn't able to contact you.

928
01:03:22,211 --> 01:03:24,811
Where are you? I'll head there now.

929
01:03:26,651 --> 01:03:27,681
Gyeol...

930
01:03:28,651 --> 01:03:30,651
says he doesn't want to go home today.

931
01:03:32,251 --> 01:03:33,721
He wants to stay with me.

932
01:03:36,161 --> 01:03:39,131
No. He has a home. Why would he stay with you?

933
01:03:39,591 --> 01:03:42,001
I'll go there. Where are you?

934
01:03:51,711 --> 01:03:54,511
- Sir, please wait a moment. - Okay.

935
01:04:04,121 --> 01:04:06,051
Let me take Gyeol. I'll carry him.

936
01:04:06,351 --> 01:04:07,491
I'll drive you home.

937
01:04:07,621 --> 01:04:09,121
The taxi's waiting.

938
01:04:10,421 --> 01:04:12,991
Just to the taxi, then.

939
01:04:38,251 --> 01:04:39,791
What kind of life have you lived?

940
01:04:48,561 --> 01:04:49,931
For the eight years since you left me,

941
01:04:52,001 --> 01:04:53,701
what kind of life have you been living?

942
01:05:26,176 --> 01:05:27,776
(Love on the Menu)

943
01:05:27,846 --> 01:05:28,846
Ma'am.

944
01:05:28,916 --> 01:05:30,416
Why are you calling me ma'am?

945
01:05:30,416 --> 01:05:32,846
Because you're not my mom, ma'am.

946
01:05:32,846 --> 01:05:34,956
Mister, why did you abandon me?

947
01:05:35,016 --> 01:05:37,056
What's this about Gyeol? Is he really not your sister's son?

948
01:05:37,056 --> 01:05:39,486
I thought Gyu Rim gave birth to Gyeol.

949
01:05:39,556 --> 01:05:40,556
She even showed me...

950
01:05:40,626 --> 01:05:42,256
a picture of him from when she was pregnant.

951
01:05:42,326 --> 01:05:43,856
She showed you an ultrasound photo?

952
01:05:44,096 --> 01:05:45,126
Where are you now?

953
01:05:45,196 --> 01:05:46,566
I never thought we'd meet like this.

954
01:05:46,566 --> 01:05:48,796
Don't you recognise me? I'm Han Gyu Oh.

955
01:05:48,866 --> 01:05:50,466
First, you need to divorce her.

956
01:05:50,536 --> 01:05:52,836
How dare you? You don't even know your place.

957
01:05:52,906 --> 01:05:55,036
That child is my eldest daughter.

958
01:05:55,776 --> 01:05:57,036
Where are you, Gyu Rim?

